"BWIGLEY" <bwigley@xtra.co.nz> writes:

> I like to use a batch file, then I don't have to type stuff in (which
> is sorta lazy). anyway:
> inside NHwiz.bat which is in my main Nethack folder:
> nethackw -u wizard -D

You could also have NH.bat that starts the game with
nethackw %1 %2 %3

so when you type
NH -u wizard -D
it starts in wizard mode, but if you just type
NH
it starts a real game.

(There is also a way to pass all given command line arguments from the
.bat to the game neater than using separate "%1 %2 %3" that limits the
number of arguments to three, but I don't remember for sure how it is
expressed.) 

